# PyIceberg client for the ldl-graph container (docker/graph/Dockerfile), installed NEXT TO
# requirements-graph.txt. No pyspark, no JVM: the container reads the Iceberg tables Spark
# publishes (gold.graph_*, pinned by tag + snapshot id) through the same Postgres JDBC catalog
# and the Silo S3 endpoint. Python 3.12 only.
#
# Lock (compiled AGAINST the core lock, so the two files agree on every shared pin; pip refuses
# the install otherwise):
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     -c requirements-graph.txt requirements-graph-spark-client.in -o requirements-graph-spark-client.txt
# Recompile whenever requirements-graph.txt changes (tests/graph/test_compose_graph.py checks it).
#
# License: Apache-2.0. The sql-postgres extra adds SQLAlchemy (MIT) and psycopg2-binary
# (LGPL-3.0 with exceptions: flagged; pg8000, BSD-3, is the permissive alternative driver).
pyiceberg[pyarrow,sql-postgres]==0.12.0
